) is=20
from computer uses.  But if they want a language to use with computers, the=
y=20
will build one to fit computers -- without all the frills that human langua=
ges=20
have.  And, for that matter, if you have to learn a new language to use a=
=20
computer, then a computer language is the way to go.  Of course, some folks=
=20
still hold out hope for being able to translate natural languages into=20
computerese, but that is a much longer shot.  So, I don't think that LoCCan=
3 is=20
going anywhere (unless Lojban gets a new Napoleon type, which leads to a=20
fragmentation again -- which will happen eventually, if the project lasts l=
ong=20
enough).
As a further strike, Lojban is looked upon as a cult language, like Klingon=
 and=20
Na'vi (and maybe Dothraki -- the first results aren't in yet) and so the pe=
ople=20
who know it and could teach it are considered flakes -- or worse.   (As a f=
lake,=20
I have to note that the Na'vi clearly have a hierarchy and a relgion, so th=
ey=20
almost inevitably have a high language and a common one. You can't talk to =
a=20
chief or a god in the same way you talk to the schlump next door.  As for=
=20
complex rules, many languages of primitive people are as bad as Sanskrit or=
=20
worse, so that isn't unrealistic.  Na'vi is a second rate conlang, but seem=
s to=20
work OK, in context and out.) =20

Don't get excited about SWH -- every version presented so far has either ha=
d=20
nothing to do with S and W or was a prima facie crock.  And usually both.





